Article 1 | Definitions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. "Project" means DH_ServerTool_JA, including its source code, scripts, documentation, and build outputs.

2. "Licensed Material" means the source code, scripts, and documentation in the Project that were independently developed by the maintainer and contributors and are separable from Third-Party Materials, together with build outputs generated from them. This License grants rights in the Licensed Material only.

3. "Original Game and Related Commercial Assets" means the following two categories together:
   (a) Original Game Assets: the game "Dread Hunger" and its official original assets (official artwork, audio, official code, trademarks, native data structures, and the like); and
   (b) Paid Commercial UE4 Assets: the paid commercial Unreal Engine 4 (UE4) assets contained in the game.

4. "Derived Files" means files made, without authorization from the applicable Lawful Rightsholders, by modifying, extracting, or repacking Original Game and Related Commercial Assets, or files inseparable from those assets because they contain their content (for example, modified or repacked .pak or .uasset asset files), regardless of who made them. The test is whether the file contains content of the Original Game and Related Commercial Assets. Merely depending on or interacting with the game at run time does not make a file "inseparable".

5. "Independent Work" means a work that its author wrote independently and that contains no part of the Licensed Material and no content of the Original Game and Related Commercial Assets, such as an independently written MOD script, plugin, or configuration. An Independent Work remains one even if it runs through the Project's loading mechanism, calls or hooks game functions at run time, or relies on objective technical facts such as memory offsets, parameter definitions, or interfaces. An Independent Work is neither a Derived File nor a Modified Version and is not governed by this License. Its copyright (limited to the author's own expression and not extending to the items in Article 2, Section 4(c)) belongs to its author. Where one work or release package contains both independently written parts and Derived Files, each part is assessed separately.

6. "Third-Party Materials" means Original Game and Related Commercial Assets, Derived Files, and general-purpose third-party open-source components unrelated to "Dread Hunger".

7. "Modified Version" means a work that contains or adapts any copyright-protected part of the Licensed Material. An Independent Work is not a Modified Version.

8. "Distribute" means to provide a copy of the Project or a Modified Version to anyone else by any means, including uploading, publishing, sharing within a group, or bundling with other content.

9. "Publicly Operate" means to run a Modified Version as a game server that is open to players at large, or for which players are recruited through a community, group, platform, server list, or similar channel. Private sessions and tests limited to you and acquaintances you invite directly, with no public recruitment, are not Public Operation.

10. "Corresponding Source" means all source code, scripts, and build configuration needed to build, install, and run a Modified Version, in the original form suited to modification (not obfuscated, encrypted, or compiled-only). It does not include Third-Party Materials or general-purpose build tools.

