   Solely to achieve technical compatibility and interoperability with the "Dread Hunger" dedicated server and community ecosystem, the Project involves, references, or is accompanied by publicly obtainable Original Game and Related Commercial Assets and related compatibility files (including Derived Files). For these:
   (a) This License grants no rights. The maintainer claims neither copyright nor exclusive control, and grants no sublicense beyond the authority of the Lawful Rightsholders.
   (b) Within the maintainer's own authority, the maintainer imposes no additional restriction on your non-commercial use, adaptation, or co-distribution of them together with the Project.
   (c) Their original ownership and lawful scope of use remain governed by the rights of the Lawful Rightsholders and applicable law. You are responsible for checking whether you may use, modify, or distribute them.
   (d) When Distributed together with the Project, Articles 4 and 5 still apply, as does the rightsholder contact channel in Section 7 of this Article.

4. What Does Not Give Rise to Independent Rights
   Under general principles of copyright law — the idea–expression dichotomy, the originality requirement, and, in jurisdictions that have such a rule, the exclusion of unlawful derivative works from protection (for example, 17 U.S.C. § 102(b) and § 103(a)) — the following do not, for purposes of this License, give rise to independent, legally protected intellectual property rights, and no community, team, or individual may rely on them to claim copyright or exclusive control:
