Article 5 | No Commercialization or Exclusivity
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Prohibited Conduct
   You may not use the Project or a Modified Version for direct or indirect commercial gain, including without limitation:
   (a) Charging for access: paid sales, paid downloads, paid archive passwords, or distribution limited to paid groups or members.
   (b) Disguised charging: making payment a condition under labels such as "sponsor unlocks" or "tip to receive source or builds", or selling setup, hosting, or maintenance packages built around the Project.
   (c) Exclusivity: making the Project or a Modified Version exclusive content of any platform, launcher, community, private server, or commercial service in order to charge fees, monetize traffic, or run a commercial operation.

2. Conduct That Does Not Violate This Article
   (a) Showing or using the Project in gameplay videos or livestreams (including default platform ad revenue and voluntary viewer tips), provided payment is never a condition of obtaining or using the Project.
   (b) Members of a non-profit self-hosted server transparently splitting server costs at actual cost.
   (c) Renting a general-purpose server or VPS and deploying the Project on it yourself.

3. Responsibility
   Legal consequences arising from a violation of this Article rest with the violator alone and have no connection to the Project or the maintainer.

